{
  "id": "Compound::DB00692 - Gene::151",
  "verbalization": "Phentolamine, a selective alpha-1 adrenergic receptor antagonist, exhibits a strong binding interaction with Adra1d, a variant of the alpha-adrenergic receptor. This binding is linked to the participation of Adra1d in Alpha-adrenergic Receptor Activity, which is subsequently participated by Adra2b. The evidence suggests that Phentolamine may influence Adra2b through a mechanism involving the activation of Adra1d, which in turn modulates the activity of Adra2b. The shared participation of Adra1d in Adrenergic Receptor Activity and Adrenoceptors further supports a potential pathway where Phentolamine's effects on Adra1d could indirectly affect Adra2b. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Adra1d as a mediator in the interaction between Phentolamine and Adra2b, emphasizing the importance of receptor heterogeneity in drug-target relationships.",
